.TH WERKMEISTER-PR 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-pr \- Open and track this workspace's PRs from its PR files (docs/workspace\-lifecycle.md)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister pr\fR [command]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Opens PRs from a workspace and tracks them to a release. Each action:
.IP \(bu 3
\fBgate\fR runs the pre\-PR gate for each PR file and changes nothing.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBgate \-\-tests\fR runs only the gate's lint and test rows, in the workspace container, on each worktree's uncommitted tree (committed, staged, unstaged and untracked changes since its base). It needs no PR file and skips the PR\-file, clean, baseline and release rows. It starts a container when none is running and stops it after. The implement stage runs it, so a failure that only happens with the container's env shows up before \fBpr open\fR.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBopen\fR gates, pushes and opens a PR for each PR file at \fBstatus: approved\fR, and records its URL. If the branch isn't pushed yet and is behind its base, \fBopen\fR rebases it onto \fBorigin/<base>\fR first when that applies with no conflict, says so in the base row, and tests the result; a conflict aborts the rebase and fails the base row. A gate that ran the lint and test rows and passed on a clean tree (\fBgate \-\-tests\fR, \fBgate\fR, or an earlier \fBopen\fR) writes \fB.werkmeister/logs/gate\-pass\-<worktree>.json\fR. Its key is the HEAD sha, the \fBorigin/<base>\fR sha and the lint and test commands. When all three still match and the tree is clean, \fBopen\fR reuses it: its tests row says so, and it runs only the PR\-file, base, clean, revert and release rows. A failed \fBgh pr create\fR keeps the record, so a retry goes straight to the create. A new commit, a base move or a changed command reruns the full gate, and so does deleting the file. A failing gate deletes it.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBpush\fR force\-pushes each open PR's branch after a rebase (rule 5's conflict fix), with \fB\-\-force\-with\-lease=<branch>:<sha>\fR where \fB<sha>\fR is the PR file's \fBconflict_head:\fR, the PR head \fBpr watch\fR's conflict wake saw (never \fBorigin/<branch>\fR as fetched, which a fetch moves onto a reviewer's commit); after the push it records the pushed head there. It refuses, pushing nothing for that PR, unless the PR file names one of the workspace's own worktrees (a worktree of a repo under the repos root; no git runs before this check, and a standalone clone, whose git config sits in the workspace, is refused), the branch is the workspace's own (\fB<user>/<workspace>\fR, or a \fBpr new\fR follow\-up once that PR settled) and checked out, the worktree is clean, the branch holds no merge commit from its base, the PR file has a \fBconflict_head:\fR, origin's branch is still that head, and the local branch once held it (its reflog), so a commit pushed before the conflict is never dropped. ICM workspaces pre\-approve it.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBautosquash\fR folds each \fBfixup!\fR (or \fBsquash!\fR/\fBamend!\fR) commit into the commit it names, in each of the workspace's own worktrees or the one named: \fBgit rebase \-\-autosquash\fR onto the merge\-base with \fBorigin/<base>\fR, with a no\-op editor and hooks off, and prints the commits left. It refuses, rewriting nothing in that worktree, unless the worktree is one of the workspace's own, has the workspace's \fB<user>/<workspace>\fR branch checked out, is clean, holds no merge commit from its base, and it has no \fBorigin/<branch>\fR tracking ref, which a push from this checkout leaves (folding a pushed commit needs a force\-push; it makes no network call). It never moves another branch (\fB\-\-no\-update\-refs\fR). A rebase that stops is aborted, and a changed tree or a \fBfixup!\fR left over fails it. ICM workspaces pre\-approve it.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBgate\fR and \fBopen\fR check free memory once, before they start a container or run a row: under \fBbudget.free_memory\fR percent available (default 15), they add a \fBmemory\fR row, read \fBretry later (low memory)\fR and exit 75 without starting anything, since Claude Code stops an idle background gate when the Mac runs low.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBgate\fR and \fBopen\fR don't wait on host load before their checks: the 1\-minute load counts the gate's own install and test rows, and the services the gate starts are already admitted against the budget. \fB\-\-no\-wait\fR is still accepted and does nothing. With tests, a gate can run past a 10\-minute tool call: run \fBpr open\fR, and \fBpr gate\fR or \fBpr gate \-\-tests\fR, as a background job with its log, as rule 3 of \fB_shared/pr\-rules.md\fR shows. \fB.werkmeister/bin/with\-temp\-home\fR runs a shorter wait (up to 90 s) before its command and exits 75 without running it if load is still over (\fBWERKMEISTER_NO_WAIT=1\fR skips it). The services a gate starts wait for room in the budget up to 30 minutes in all, keeping their place in the queue, then fail with \fBNO_CAPACITY\fR. They fail at once when only holders waiting on a person with a run in flight could make room, naming each and the step that frees it (answer its question, or stop it from the pane); one that costs more CPUs or memory than the whole budget fails at once with \fBNEVER_FITS\fR, naming its cost and the budget for the first resource over, as does \fBfeature up\fR. A start that runs a setup service (the install) first waits up to 90 s while the host load is over \fBbudget.host_load\fR or free memory is under \fBbudget.free_memory\fR, then fails with \fBHOST_LOAD\fR; \fBWERKMEISTER_NO_WAIT=1\fR skips that wait, \fB\-\-no\-wait\fR does not, and on macOS and Windows the load is the Docker VM's. A failed check ends with the host load. A test row killed with exit 137, or whose only error is vitest's worker RPC timeout (\fBTimeout calling "onTaskUpdate"\fR, a worker blocked past vitest's fixed 60 s), is run once more, after the same host\-load wait \fBwith\-temp\-home\fR runs, and says it was retried; it fails only if the retry fails too. A red test row whose only failures are timeouts (that RPC timeout, or a test that timed out), ending with host load over \fBbudget.host_load\fR, ends with \fBfailed under host load N (over L): rerun\fR and the gate exits 75.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBstatus\fR records merged, shipped or closed from GitHub and the repo's release tags.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBadopt\fR records a PR opened outside the workspace.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBwatch\fR resumes each opening session once its PR merges, ships or closes; \fB\-\-install\fR schedules it.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBnew\fR starts a follow\-up PR file and branch for a worktree whose PRs have merged.
.PP
Inside a workspace, \fBgh pr create\fR (and so \fB/create\-pr\fR) is blocked by a PreToolUse hook; \fBwerkmeister pr open\fR is the way to open a PR. The full process (PR files, the gate, ship detection, the PR guard) is in docs/workspace\-lifecycle.md.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
werkmeister pr gate
werkmeister pr gate \-\-tests
werkmeister pr open
werkmeister pr status \-\-json
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBwerkmeister workspace close\fR ends the workspace once its PRs have shipped.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
